  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "English | [简体中文](README.zh.md)"
    },
    {
      "section": "WebScout",
      "text": "Tavily-backed web search (Search) and page fetch (Fetch) for DeepSeek Harness —\nwith a clean, two-column settings card."
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "- **Search provider** `webscout`: Tavily `/search` with depth, topic, time range,\n  answer mode, raw content, domains, country, images, retries and an optional\n  result cache.\n- **Fetch provider** `webscout-fetch`: one provider that can read a page through\n  Tavily Extract, Firecrawl, or a direct HTTP request.\n- **Key rotation**: several credential references form a ring; a key that keeps\n  failing sits out for 60 seconds.\n- **Fallback**: delegate to the built-in DeepSeek provider when Tavily is\n  unreachable (optional).\n- **Settings card**: live quota from Tavily `/usage`, connection test, search\n  and fetch controls, and an advanced section for everything else."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```sh\ndsh plugin --profile <profile> add \"file:/path/to/dsh-webscout\"\n```\n\nThe bundle patch elects `webscout` for search and `webscout-fetch` for fetch, so\nthe card never writes the web service's config entry."
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "Open **Settings → Plugins → WebScout search**. The card edits the plugin's own\n`webscout` section; the API key is stored in the local credential store under\n`TAVILY_API_KEY` (or the reference you configure)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Search fields",
      "text": "| Field | Default | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `maxResults` | 5 | 1–20 |\n| `searchDepth` | basic | basic / advanced / fast / ultra-fast |\n| `topic` | general | general / news / finance |\n| `includeAnswer` | true | false / true / basic / advanced |\n| `includeRawContent` | false | false / markdown / text |\n| `chunksPerSource` | 3 | 1–3 |\n| `timeRange` | — | day / week / month / year |\n| `days` | — | recency window in days |\n| `includeDomains` / `excludeDomains` | — | comma or space separated |\n| `country` | — | country boost |\n| `cacheTtlSeconds` | 0 | 0 disables the cache |\n| `cacheMaxEntries` | 200 | LRU cap |\n| `cacheBypassFresh` | true | skip cache for news/finance/time-windowed queries |\n| `engine` | tavily | tavily or deepseek |\n| `fallbackEngine` | none | none or deepseek |\n| `citeFormat` | plain | plain or footnote |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Fetch fields",
      "text": "| Field | Default | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `fetchMode` | tavily | tavily / http / firecrawl |\n| `firecrawlApiKeyEnv` | FIRECRAWL_API_KEY | credential reference |\n| `firecrawlBaseURL` | https://api.firecrawl.dev/v1 | endpoint base |"
    },
    {
